{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Pinchas son of Elazar son of Aharon the priest.</b> Because the tribes were disparaging him — 'Have you seen this son of Puti, whose mother's father fattened calves for idolatry, and he killed a prince of a tribe of Israel?' Therefore Scripture comes and traces his lineage after Aharon (Sanhedrin 82a)." "<b>When he avenged My vengeance.</b> By avenging My vengeance — by expressing the indignation that was Mine to express. Every term of קִנְאָה is competing to avenge a matter; אנפרטמנט בְּלַעַ\"ז."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French espertement (or enfortement), 'zealously / vigorously'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:45.098571941Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}